        "id": "W19.FACTION.REED",
        "name": "The Reedwater Compact",
        "status": "authored_working_definition",
        "body": "**Civic foundation.** A federation of basin tenders, growers, emergence operators and adjoining households. Crown Basin is its reference settlement. Catchment councils coordinate scarce usable water, working perches and supply routes; private enclosures and independent Wrangloids coexist with shared facilities.\n\n**Why the sport matters.** The full life of a component is visible here: a juvenile, an intact adult, a fitted array, then an aerial racer. The sport makes careful raising and skillful construction public achievements. It also supports ordinary ground racers who buy the region’s timing or reserve stock.\n\n**Representative institution.** The Basin Race Council runs Crown Trials and keeps public course and result records. Its ecological/maintenance role is distinct from its sporting role. It may restrict access to an occupied working enclosure or announce a habitat closure for a real stated cause; it cannot grant exclusive permission to know, own or breed a species. Equivalent lawful acquisition and paid grow-out remain possible elsewhere.\n\n**Support package.** The representative’s existing committed brood can be boarded with named capacity and endpoints; the faction does not require the representative to donate it. Array transport, arrival matching and a declared reserve-stock allowance are booked through actual operators. Care includes the return journey and an agreed contingency, not merely departure.\n\n**Construction culture.** Exposed wing-sweep diagrams, clear stage labels, natural veining and shaped supports. Quadwing and Longwing both appear, with ground-foundation kits beside them. Published control and duty differences matter more than calling every long wing an endurance upgrade.\n\n**Selection occasion.** Crown Trials race entrants through legal route choices and repeated usable maneuvers. An easy-to-observe court or mating display is not an examination for a racing berth. The final winner, not the keeper of the most expensive nursery, represents the faction.\n\n**Internal pressure.** A headline meeting can consume the same space required by uninterruptible emergence. The council must book visiting arrival space rather than evict late-stage stock. Specialists can earn through extra capacity and matching; the default novice package still arrives ready for ordinary assembly.\n\n**Relations.** The Commons supplies root support, Traverse carries stage-sensitive stock, and Lantern supplies specialist buyers. Reedwater’s dependence on imported structural and prepared-drive stock prevents the faction from becoming a self-sufficient 'water plus flight' bonus package.\n\n**Emblem and objects.** An open ring crossed by a single curved reed. Gates carry the ring as a venue identifier, not as a player-only boost. The characteristic object is an emergence reservation board that leads to a physical array case, with a separate public roster for the race.",
