        "id": "W19.CHARTER.COMPACT",
        "name": "The Derby Compact: a limited sporting agreement",
        "status": "authored_working_definition",
        "body": "The four described factions and New World City’s host administration recognize a shared finish, a way to qualify, ordinary inspection, record exchange and responsibilities for advertised support. This proposed **Derby Compact** governs the programme it sanctions. It is not a peace treaty, universal licensing authority, global bank or explanation of every faction’s laws.\n\nThe **Circuit Registry** records which events confer advancement and whether an entrant has earned it. The **Stewards’ Table** hears sporting disputes under published procedures. The **Host Works Office** contracts the city’s physical venue, receiving capacity and event labor. No one office simultaneously sells the entrants their parts, selects a favorite winner and reviews its own complaint.\n\nOrdinary informal races and shops can exist outside Compact sanction. They produce real local outcomes and enjoyment. They cannot advertise a Derby berth unless that consequence is actually recognized. The point of recognition is shared trust in a specific result, not permission to run a roach in a gutter.\n\nA source record, product qualification, maker advertisement and race result remain different claims. Race officials inspect capability and the actual fitted entry. They do not demand research-grade ancestry for every organ, and no manufacturer owns the assimilation interface.\n\nThe Compact is intentionally narrow enough to let disagreeing societies compete. It protects a common start and finish while leaving who breeds, what people collect, and which local styles they enjoy open.",
