      {
        "id": "W19.MEET.RIVET",
        "name": "Cinderhouse / Rivet Reach Regional",
        "status": "authored_working_definition",
        "body": "**Level and purpose.** A Regional programme for Local-qualified lanistas in the chosen discipline. Its reference Ground Open edition uses the M4 series. It is a new event family, not a rewritten past prototype result.\n\n**Construction.** Two published layouts alternate: a loaded-rise route with broad restarts, and a longer run with an abrasive rail and a fully disclosed landing. A smooth bypass around the roughest insert trades distance for different contact demands. The configurations use real owned or booked pieces and a common event inspection.\n\n**Actual choices.** Torque, Lowstep and adequate support can help a loaded body restart. A lighter high-cadence construction can gain on the long run. A rail guide is useful when the line touches the rail; a clean inner line can avoid that particular loss. Braking and a more controlled approach provide alternatives to simply making a longer jump.\n\n**Progression.** The series winner earns the affiliated faction’s corresponding final entry. Winning this regional does not itself award the Rivet Commons seat to a visitor representing another faction. Other valid competitors retain their results and any actual prize.\n\n**Community use.** Nonqualifying public heats and bench bookings occupy a separate programme. Ordinary residents do not lose their only local course merely because the regional ceremony is present. Section crews, receiving staff and ordinary suppliers are paid for actual work.",
