        "status": "authored_working_definition",
        "body": "**Level and purpose.** A Regional Flyer programme reached through a Local Flyer win, not through a Ground Open badge alone. A separately scheduled ground event may share the venue infrastructure but does not share the aerial grid.\n\n**Construction.** The reference M4 layouts adapt Foundry Courtyard and Reed Sweep principles: an understandable gate loop, a gradual outer climb, a direct steeper choice, broad forward travel and a receiving apron after the scored finish. Route openings, allowed retries and airflow conditions are public.\n\n**Actual choices.** Longwing can exploit sustained travel and its real folding arrangement; Quadwing can use an appropriately built redirection capability. These are tendencies to test, not automatic species matchups. Efficient drive and suitable delivery can improve either. A ventral brake contributes only at an actual surface, while aerial slowing needs an actual force or air interaction.\n\n**Progression.** The valid series winner receives a Factional Flyer entry under the recorded affiliation. First-flight demonstrations, timetabled coaching and public display remain separate, complete activities with no need to enter the qualifier.\n\n**Source demand.** Conditioned arrays, matching work, supported roots, reserves and stage-aware receiving matter. A competitor may arrive with a complete tin. No requirement to reproduce its aquatic or colony supply chain personally is imposed as evidence of competence.",
