      {
        "id": "W19.MEET.LANTERN",
        "name": "Saltglass / Lantern Lines programme",
        "status": "authored_working_definition",
        "body": "**Level and purpose.** A venue family with separately advertised Regional Speedsters, Fireworks and local display dates. One poster must not imply that a display award qualifies a racer or that all entries share the same equipment policy.\n\n**Construction.** The ground pattern alternates a broad shared straight, a readable chicane, and a choice between a tighter short route and a longer open turn. Aerial dates use Lantern Exchange geometry with actual upper/lower route volumes and a visible merge. The operator books separate safe physical spaces or times rather than intersecting two active races for atmosphere.\n\n**Actual choices.** Quick-release feet and useful correction support fast changes, but do not replace drive. A Fireworks variant offers aligned approaches and escape routes rather than a kill corridor with no positional alternatives. A converted Counterbrace is inspected as its actual support-only preparation, not accepted simply because the player promises not to close a weapon.\n\n**Progression.** A Regional winner in each racing discipline earns only that discipline’s Factional entry. Display participants receive their own result and recognition. Both can become interesting to a maker or customer, but neither creates a guaranteed sale.\n\n**Material culture.** Complete tins, natural-pattern specimens, rematched arrays and annotated used components share a market. Their actual condition and purpose are legible beside the event. A specialist contact order requests measured release/purchase; a collector can request appearance without inventing a performance benefit.",
