        "body": "**Level and purpose.** A Regional meeting hosted by a travelling crew using announced laid versions. Each discipline has its own roster and recorded result. Travelling character comes from construction and people, not surprise changes to eligibility.\n\n**Construction.** A receiving yard holds the section library, an approachable practice loop and the competition route. A smooth layout emphasizes uninterrupted running and genuine fast builds; an alternate uses a fully described small rise and broad recovery run. The course remains fixed within each heat. There is no secret repair defect that only locals know how to avoid.\n\n**Actual choices.** Sound sleeves, stable support and an appropriate approach can preserve motion. A prepared recovery mechanism can recover from a relevant posture but earns no points itself. A racer that stays upright and runs faster can win without it. More portable hardware is a transport choice, not a universal speed advantage.\n\n**Progression and contingency.** The Regional winner proceeds under their recorded affiliation. A venue closure activates an announced alternate or a rescheduled window with practical support; results already completed remain identified. An unavailable final is not scored as a loss for everybody who could not arrive at the replacement immediately.\n\n**Local value.** Course lending, packing, fitting and household hospitality can provide actual paid work. Competitors are not compelled to finish those jobs before their own race. A visitor who comes only to sell a well-made tin is still participating in the hobby.",
