      {
        "id": "W19.MEET.FACTIONAL",
        "name": "Four factional finals; one sporting basis",
        "status": "authored_working_definition",
        "body": "**Common eligibility.** A Regional winner, correct campaign affiliation, eligible ready host, and the declared discipline. The reference final has four entrants and one primary representative place. Where the qualified field is larger, advertised preliminary racing determines the four. No workshop judge substitutes a preferred sponsored entrant.\n\n**Common Bench Final — Rivet Commons.** An M4 programme alternates mixed ground or equivalent declared aerial layouts with a common service interval. Shared work tables let spectators recognize real changes. It is not a judged build-off; the series winner earns the seat.\n\n**Crown Trials — Reedwater Compact.** The appropriate ground or Flyer M4 programme exposes supply, working-root and controlled-recovery differences. Stage-care and receiving demonstrations occur alongside it, without contributing points. The winner and standby receive booked biological support.\n\n**Lantern Exchange Final — Lantern Exchange.** Racing and appearance display have separate judges and result records. Public build cards can be shared with permission; private pedigrees are not forcibly published as a condition of the berth. The racing winner and standby are recorded before commercial invitations.\n\n**Moving Final — Traverse Freeholds.** A published portable layout travels to the declared host yard. Its relocation procedure and reserve venue are part of entry information. Winning confers the same standing as any fixed-hall final; itinerant origin is not a lower class of qualification.\n\nEach final records a primary winner and a ranked eligible standby. A tied standby position uses the same advertised sporting tie-break, not a donor’s bid. All four cultures can support fast, offensive, restrained or aerial constructions within the relevant rules. The faction identity changes the people and resources around the racer, not how its tissue is scored.",
