      },
      {
        "id": "W19.MEET.DERBY",
        "name": "The What’s Left of the World Derby",
        "status": "authored_working_definition",
        "body": "**Reference field.** One earned representative from each of the four described signatories per active discipline. Standbys replace genuinely unavailable delegates before the published cutoff, not after seeing whether a first heat was favorable. A larger future signatory field requires a separately published qualifying programme.\n\n**Public headliners.** Ground Open is the central ground title; Flyer Open is the aerial headline. Speedsters and Fireworks receive their own titles where staged. There is no comparison converting flight time, ground time and destructive effect into one fictitious universal champion score. Open remains the most famous construction class in the public framing.\n\n**Sporting resolution.** Equal-exposure preparation and declared seeding precede a single final per discipline. The first valid finisher wins that final. Actual ties use the announced rerun with unchanged qualifying standing and an ordinary refit/inspection interval. A no-contest does not produce a title. The full intended final is simultaneous physical racing, not a claim that the historical pair solver already supports it.\n\n**Course character.** The ground championship combines long pace runs, legible shared traffic, a disclosed surface change and at least two approach opportunities. The aerial championship combines actual height, broad passing, clear gates and one meaningful alternative route. No exclusive organ is made the only way to finish. Novel builds must satisfy actual validity, not conform to the silhouette on the festival poster.\n\n**Material consequence.** A prize is actual money, stock, service or object under advertised terms. A large cup, a faction banner and a breeder’s publication can all commemorate the result but do not improve inherited characteristics. A recorded winning build can support a maker inquiry, not guarantee descendants or copy its anatomy.\n\n**Afterward.** The champion retains the animal, line records and personal projects they actually own. The host city remains a place for ordinary participation, and the returning hometown retains its own identity. The final closes a campaign without deleting the rest of the hobby.",
