        "body": "A new Spanrest craftsperson who prepares and rematches existing joint stock. Len rents Foldout Club bench time, buys or receives particular linings, and returns customers’ hosts and retained components after agreed work. A customer job and the fitter’s own specimen collection are separate inventories.\n\nLen’s expertise concerns working travel and contamination under known conditions. It does not reveal wild genomes, guarantee every mixed-source pair, or confer authority over regional inspection. The personal product line, Bridgejoint, records fit ranges and preparation revisions. Brood supply comes from cooperating keepers unless Len actually operates the required nursery.\n\nThis role supports ordinary paid work, remembered clients, testing advice and kit supply without requiring a championship career. It is not a new protected profession or a claim that every Traverse resident knows the same craft.",
