        "id": "W19.HISTORY.FRAME",
        "name": "Hobby-year dating and the meaning of an original",
        "status": "authored_working_definition",
        "body": "The following three histories are new fictional reference cases, not recovered past events or simulated sales. **H0** denotes the founding-rivalry era; **H30** denotes the current thirty-years-later setting at the resolution of this working timeline. These are hobby-year labels, not Earth dates, proof that the apocalypse was thirty years ago, or exact birthday records.\n\nA lineage, an individual, an extracted core, a prepared component, a fitted build, a guide, and a printed tin can each have a history. Do not use a single 'original' flag for all of them. A maintained line can span several animal generations without requiring a founder to remain alive for the entire thirty-year history.\n\nThese case records are content authored for the bible. They do not add animals or transactions to a player save. When later instantiated, every living object needs the same custody, anatomy and condition treatment as other stock. Archived observations can remain after the source is no longer living.",
